[32m+[m[32m### Phase 2 Timing Optimisation[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPost-route path inspection showed that the original 100 MHz limiter was not[m
[32m+[m[32mthe DSP. It ran from data BRAM through LOAD write-back, MEM/WB-to-EX[m
[32m+[m[32mforwarding, the BEQ comparison, and redirect/flush logic to a fetch-buffer[m
[32m+[m[32mpayload reset input. Its 9.339 ns data delay was 4.113 ns logic (44.040%) and[m
[32m+[m[32m5.226 ns routing (55.960%) across nine levels.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe accepted experimental core, `cpu_core_pipeline_mac8_timingopt`, keeps the[m
[32m+[m[32mverified baseline intact and clears only frontend valid bits during dynamic[m
[32m+[m[32mbubbles and redirects. Invalid PC/instruction payload registers retain[m
[32m+[m[32mdon't-care data; reset behaviour and valid instruction loading are unchanged.[m
[32m+[m[32mThis removes the long redirect cone from payload data/reset inputs without a[m
[32m+[m[32mnew stage or architectural change.[m
