[32m+[m[32m### MAC8 Post-Route Timing Optimisation[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe original 100 MHz post-route critical path was inspected from the preserved[m
[32m+[m[32mcheckpoint before RTL changes. It starts at the data RAMB18E1[m
[32m+[m[32m`CLKBWRCLK`, passes through LOAD write-back selection, MEM/WB-to-EX forwarding,[m
[32m+[m[32mthe 32-bit BEQ comparison, and redirect/flush logic, and ends at[m
[32m+[m[32m`fetch_buffer_instruction_reg[15]/R`. WNS is `+0.031 ns`; the 9.339 ns data[m
[32m+[m[32mdelay is 4.113 ns logic (44.040%) and 5.226 ns routing (55.960%) over nine[m
[32m+[m[32mlogic levels. The DSP path is near-critical but is not the original absolute[m
[32m+[m[32mlimiter.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe accepted experimental core is[m
[32m+[m[32m`rtl/cpu_core_pipeline_mac8_timingopt.sv`, with the matching top[m
[32m+[m[32m`rtl/fpga_top_pipeline_mac8_timingopt.sv`. Reset still initializes frontend[m
[32m+[m[32mpayloads, while redirect/bubble invalidation clears only valid bits and leaves[m
[32m+[m[32minvalid payload data as don't-care state. The baseline[m
[32m+[m[32m`rtl/cpu_core_pipeline_full.sv` is unchanged.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCandidate XSim commands used `-d MAC8_TIMINGOPT_DUT` so the existing[m
